.TH MU2EREQUESTSENDER 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2e-pcie-utils 9.01.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2eRequestSender \- send readout/data requests to a DTC from the software CFO
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2eRequestSender
.RB [ \-n
.IR num ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR ts ]
.RB [ \-i ]
.RB [ \-d
.IR us ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-q ]
.RB [ \-h ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Constructs a default
.B DTCLib::DTC
(card
.B DTCLIB_DTC
or 0, ROC mask 0x1, full initialisation) and a
.B DTCSoftwareCFO
that sends requests over DMA.
With
.B \-n
greater than 1 it sends a range of requests starting at tag
.BR \-o ,
otherwise a single request.
The usage text calls the program
.BR requestSender .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-n " num"
Number of requests (default 1).
.TP
.BI \-o " ts"
Starting event-window tag (default 1).
.TP
.B \-i
Do not increment the tag.
.TP
.BI \-d " us"
Delay between requests.
.TP
.BI \-c " n"
Debug packets per request.
.TP
.B \-q
Quiet.
.TP
.B \-h
Usage, exit 0.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0; library exceptions abort the process.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.BR DTCLIB_DTC ,
.BR DTCLIB_SIM_ENABLE .
.SH WARNINGS
The DTC object is constructed before the options are parsed, so even
.B \-h
initialises the card: ROC mask 0x1 disables links 1\-5 and their ROC emulators,
clears SERDES loopback, and clears the CFO-emulation bit.
Never run it on a card in a running partition.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
DTCLIB_DTC=1 mu2eRequestSender \-n 100 \-o 0x1000 \-d 100
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2eUtil (1),
.BR libDTCInterface (3)
